WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.640
Grimm was a show that defied the&nbsp;
odds during its six-season run.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.600
While Constantine and other supernatural sagas&nbsp;
came and went like a whisper in the wind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.880
Grimm persevered, due in no small part to&nbsp;
the series attracting a loyal fan base who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.240
fell for its magical enchantments and&nbsp;
dark — some might say grim — charms.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.200
NBC's folklore-inspired procedural follows&nbsp;
Nick Burkhardt, a Portland detective and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.440
the descendent of a long line of monster&nbsp;
hunters called Grimms — a reference to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.360
the fairy-tale scribes, the Brothers&nbsp;
Grimm, whose work inspired the show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.400
As the titular Grimm, Burkhardt has the power&nbsp;
to see through the human masks worn by Wesen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.080
an ancient race of anthropomorphic beasts with&nbsp;
a wide array of magical abilities. When Wesen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.680
become irritated, stressed, or aggressive, they&nbsp;
undergo an accidental transformation that reveals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.840
their true form - which is where Burkhardt&nbsp;
and his team of monster hunters come in.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:54.960
"I thought he was going to kill me."

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.320
"Why?"

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.600
"He's a Grimm. It's what they do.”

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.920
"A what?"

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:02.880
"A Grimm."

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.760
Although the series never dazzled in the ratings,&nbsp;
it drew enough of a committed following to carry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.760
on for the better part of the decade. But&nbsp;
alas, like all good things in this world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:18.240
the cult series had to come to an end eventually.&nbsp;
So what prompted NBC to drop the cancelation ax?

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.520
Surprisingly, it came about in part&nbsp;
because the show's creators felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.000
like they didn't really have anything left to say.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.240
While NBC ultimately made the decision&nbsp;
to cut Grimm from the schedule,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.480
showrunners James Kouf and David Greenwalt&nbsp;
told TV Line that they felt like they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.960
running out of material that&nbsp;
would keep the show fresh.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.800
For that reason, they weren't even&nbsp;
really upset by the cancelation. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.600
the creators recalled feeling panic when they&nbsp;
thought season 6 would be renewed for 22 episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.640
breathing a sigh of relief when the network only&nbsp;
called for 13. That limited order turned out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.920
be a blessing, as the final season boasted&nbsp;
a rich, mythology-laden storyline that might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.360
not have felt nearly so satisfying if it had&nbsp;
been stretched out to a full 22-episode season.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.200
Fortunately for the fans and everyone&nbsp;
involved in the show's creation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.760
Grimm got to say goodbye on a high note,&nbsp;
with a satisfying conclusion that wrapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:13.680
up the existing plotlines and put a nice cherry&nbsp;
on top of its story. Series star David Giuntoli&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.400
told TV Line that they were happy to get that&nbsp;
chance, as many shows get cancelled without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.680
having the opportunity to truly finish their&nbsp;
stories in a way that is creatively satisfying.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.880
It might have helped that Grimm was part of&nbsp;
a larger zeitgeist. One part urban fantasy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.680
one part police procedural, the show owed&nbsp;
as much of a creative to debt to Buffy the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:39.280
Vampire Slayer as it does to Law &amp; Order. As a&nbsp;
result, it felt like an oddball in NBC's lineup.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.880
But Grimm had good company elsewhere,&nbsp;
debuting in a season that was crowded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:48.000
with fairy tale-inspired content. While NBC was&nbsp;
revving up the marketing engine behind Grimm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.400
ABC was pushing its own buzzy new&nbsp;
fairy tale riff, Once Upon a Time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:58.000
Both shows defied their middling reviews to live&nbsp;
a full life on their respective networks. Heck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.840
after Grimm was canceled, Once Upon&nbsp;
a Time carried on for another year!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.520
And unusually, Grimm actually saw a ratings&nbsp;
bump in its final season. While season five hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:14.400
a series low, averaging 5.97 million viewers,&nbsp;
season six rose to 6.07 million. And that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.880
apparently enough to convince NBC there might&nbsp;
be more stories to wring out of the concept yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.200
as a Grimm spinoff series with a&nbsp;
female lead was announced in 2018.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.680
So far, no further details have been announced,&nbsp;
although some of Grimm's cast members confirmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.800
in a YouTube Q&amp;A for WIzard World that there have&nbsp;
been some ongoing discussions behind the scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:38.320
about their characters returning. And with Grimm&nbsp;
and Once Upon a Time now both gone, it seems like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:44.320
there's a fairy tale procedural-sized hole in the&nbsp;
network TV ecosystem just waiting to be filled.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.640
Here's hoping they jump&nbsp;
down that rabbit hole soon.

